    "hypothesis": "Compilation fails because the binding file registers functions with the same names as the C++ wrapper functions, causing pybind11 to interpret the address as an overloaded function set. The raw launcher functions in custom_ops.cu are declared extern \"C\" but the wrapper functions in custom_ops_binding.cpp share the same identifier names (relu_sqrt_forward, silu_forward, mha_forward). Inside register_custom_ops, `&relu_sqrt_forward` is an overloaded function name and template argument deduction fails. The fix is to rename the wrapper functions to avoid collision with the raw launchers (e.g., relu_sqrt_forward_py, silu_forward_py, mha_forward_py) and update the registration and model_new.py calls accordingly.",
    "evidence": [
      "Error log shows: 'couldn’t deduce template parameter ‘Func’' when calling m.def with &relu_sqrt_forward, &silu_forward, &mha_forward.",
      "The .cpp file declares extern \"C\" functions with identical names to the local wrapper functions, causing overloaded name sets.",
      "Pybind11 m.def requires a concrete function pointer; overloaded functions need static_cast or non-overloaded names."
    ],
    "changes": [
      "Rename wrapper functions in custom_ops_binding.cpp to relu_sqrt_forward_py, silu_forward_py, mha_forward_py.",
      "Update register_custom_ops to use the new wrapper function names.",
      "Update model_new.py to call cuda_extension.relu_sqrt_forward_py, cuda_extension.silu_forward_py, cuda_extension.mha_forward_py.",
      "Keep the raw launcher names unchanged in custom_ops.cu."
    ]
